{"type": "text", "timestamp": 1791580549757, "sessionID": "ses_edd7b45d1ffeDMzacbBWfF6Rwp", "part": {"id": "prt_122858aa3001gQKZMsSBB47ibH", "messageID": "msg_1228584b10011yQRiytAL1ap8c", "sessionID": "ses_edd7b45d1ffeDMzacbBWfF6Rwp", "type": "text", "text": "Completed using actual Lykoi MCP calls. **CallerA\u2019s active behavior was replaced through an explicit family migration; CallerB was retained.**\n\n### Successors and immutable pins\n\nBoth successors retain revision 1 and their original signatures.\n\n```text\nMinimumLoad successor\nfd2fc17ed5fdc1a5742f610a2cb51b53e2f6bd20832b258692d28d26c3fff8b9\n\nActive CallerA successor\neaa72562b96506047decbd07f77a793e6b68091403414fcfc35d4ed6804e3bdc\n\nRetained CallerB\n5e09e67aee298422d290ac9bf214a1938103fd60a2fc016f9d7e35066bfbd490\n```\n\n`MinimumLoad` was admitted against exact predecessor:\n```text\nd357f298d9ba18ac40c428d3f493203c2888bcc72bac6f9df9aba095445f6b49\n```\n\nIt now computes `((x+y)+y)+3` with checked Int64 addition. Both original checks were preserved exactly, including order, dependency lists, codes, and sites:\n1. `g1`: `floor<=x`, `FIRST_MINIMUM`, site `x`.\n2. `g2`: `floor<=y`, `SECOND_MINIMUM`, site `y`.\n\nCallerA\u2019s successor changes **only** its `MinimumLoad` dependency pin and compose-call identity. All other structure remains unchanged.\n\n### Explicit migration\n\nThe registry accepted the total family decision:\n- Original CallerA \u2192 CallerA successor.\n- CallerB \u2192 `null` / retain.\n\nMigration status: **`migrated`**.\n\n### Retrieval, validation, and execution\n\nRetrieved both active caller closures and confirmed the recorded migration. Validation returned:\n- **Active CallerA:** valid, 12 expanded nodes.\n- **Retained CallerB:** valid, 10 expanded nodes; still pinned to original `MinimumLoad`.\n\nActual executions, with hexadecimal inputs/outputs and zero-based offsets:\n\n| Caller | Input | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Active A | `151e` | 89 \u2192 `0059` |\n| Active A | `1515` | 71 \u2192 `0047` |\n| Active A | `1414` | `FIRST_MINIMUM`, offset 0, `g1` |\n| Active A | `1514` | `SECOND_MINIMUM`, offset 1, `g2` |\n| Active A | `141400` | `TRAILING`, offset 2, `input_end` |\n| Active A | `15` | `TRUNCATED`, offset 1, `read_y` |\n| Retained B | `15` | 86 \u2192 `0056` |\n| Retained B | `ff` | 788 \u2192 `0314` |\n| Retained B | `14` | `FIRST_MINIMUM`, offset 0, original `g1` |\n| Retained B | `1400` | `TRAILING`, offset 1, `input_end` |\n| Original A | `151e` | 77 \u2192 `004d` |\n\nThe original CallerA still executes its original closure, and CallerB continues executing the original `MinimumLoad`. Predecessor definitions remain immutable. No calls failed in this stage.", "time": {"start": 1791580539555, "end": 1791580549755}, "metadata": {"openai": {"itemId": "msg_020d4cd7c553af41016ac9597c7ee087d096cb486a822c5015", "phase": "final_answer"}}}}
